WEBVTT

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.650
What a nice hot bath.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.910
It's good to go on a cruise every so often.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.440
Now if only I didn't have to work...

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.880
Stay still, Grenda.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.300
You need to make sure to use shampoo.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.300
Don't wanna!

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.380
Don't!

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.930
I-I'm sorry.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.140
Are you all right?

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.790
Hey now, how could we be all right?

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.100
Huh? You...

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.060
Kirasaka-san?

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.900
Yuiri, what happened?

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.280
What about Grenda?

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.910
Huh?!

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.000
How come you're here, Kirasaka?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.820
That's supposed to be my question!

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.000
We're escorting that girl to Itogami Island.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.460
What about you?

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.840
On a secret investigation for MAR.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.870
"MAR"?

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.050
You mean that international magic corporation?

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:09.550
The heck just happened?

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.060
Don't tell me we're stranded?

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.060
Yuiri!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.310
Lots of ships!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.440
What's going on?!

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.870
<i>The town was called Itogami Island.</i>

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:42.210
<i>An artificial island constructed of carbon fiber, resin, metal, and magic floating on the Pacific Ocean.</i>

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.800
<i>It functions as a habitat and a special administrative region for demons.</i>

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.840
<i>There lived a certain boy.</i>

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.710
<i>The Fourth Progenitor.</i>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.180
<i>A fourth progenitor who's not even supposed to exist.</i>

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:05.270
<i>According to the legend, he's to become aware of his empire, and act as an emperor who reigns over the world.</i>

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.240
<i>His name is...</i>

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.990
<i>Akatsuki Kojou.</i>

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:44.660
I'm beat.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.170
I just came back from the mainland.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.630
And I already need to go to school?

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.360
Morning, Kojou-kun.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.230
What's with you? Put on some clothes, quickly!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.570
Idling around a teenage lady naked is a crime.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.740
Sorry.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.930
Your shirt is on the dining chair.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.890
C'mon, just put it on!

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.700
I get it.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.540
The same goes for you.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.640
Huh?

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:30.450
Huh?!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.670
D-Did you see?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.370
Huh? We're out of milk?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.380
Ignoring me?!

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:40.390
I used it for the scrambled eggs.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:43.670
You did? What am I gonna drink now?

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.460
Whatever, I'll go and buy some.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.820
Good luck with that.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:50.360
Huh?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:57.320
After the successive cancellations of trade ships, many stores on the island cannot remain open.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.360
Right... There was some freighter accident.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.320
Many of them.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.240
They've been running out of stock in no time lately.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.670
What can you do?

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:04.290
This is a man-made island we're living on.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.910
I'll check if I can find some after school with Himeragi.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.670
You'll be with Yukina-chan today too...?

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.550
Hm? Something wrong?

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.640
Uh, no.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.630
It's always like that.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.350
Nagisa-chan said that?

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.050
She's been acting strange since we came back from the mainland.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.570
Um... I can't really put it into words.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.780
With all the things that happened, 
it's no wonder if she's still in a bit of a shock.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.700
Well, certainly many things happened.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.660
Even Asagi found out about it.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.370
By the way, was everything all right?

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.200
I'd say yeah.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:55.290
She asked all those strange questions on the way back, and I blurted out everything though.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.090
Ah, right.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.050
That time, I had to explain about you too.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.350
So I accidentally told her about the Lion King Organization and stuff.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.690
You okay with that?

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.420
I don't think it's a problem.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:10.790
I do have permission to reveal 
my identity if deemed necessary.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:12.000
I see.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:18.080
I made sure she knows you wouldn't be with me all the time if it weren't your duty.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.570
I wouldn't, you say?

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:22.780
Is that so?

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.830
Huh?

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.230
What's wrong, Himeragi?

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:28.170
You're really insensitive, aren't you?

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.930
Not like I didn't know though.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:30.560
What?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.900
Himeragi, wait.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.290
Hey!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.720
With Nagisa and Himeragi like that, this is going to be a tough day...

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.050
Morning, Fourth Progenitor.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.130
Hey!

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:47.850
Just kidding.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.250
Morning, Kojou.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.740
Morning.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.710
What's with the soft vibes with you two right at the start of the day?

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.520
Orin?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.600
S-Soft vibes my ass.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.820
Right, Asagi?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.610
Y-Yeah.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:07.580
Um, we just came back from the mainland, so we're really tired is all.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:08.650
What?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:09.990
Just the two of you went to the mainland?

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.790
Does that mean...?

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.490
Kojou, you dumbass!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.230
Just so you know, it's not like that.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:16.740
It's not what you think, Orin.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.130
Really?

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.610
'Sup.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:22.050
Why're you fighting from the start of the day?

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.170
We aren't!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:25.930
Whatever.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.760
Here, a souvenir from Tokyo.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.470
What gives? You went to the mainland too?

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.100
I had my reasons, you know.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.600
Anyway, I'm beat.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:42.460
Well, at any rate, 
it's good you all made it back safely.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:43.770
What do you mean?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.340
Akatsuki-kun, don't you feel anything off,
 looking around this classroom?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.320
Huh?

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:53.540
Come to think of it, there's a lot of latecomers.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.540
Bingo.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:08:01.230
None of the ships that set off for
 Itogami Island arrived since yesterday,

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.670
be it for having an accident,
 getting stranded, or whatever.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.660
The planes aren't in operation either,
 for turbulent air or whatnot.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.550
Those are to blame.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:09.760
For real?

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.140
For real.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.970
What a coincidence.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.810
Coincidence my ass.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.600
Let's hope for the best.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.650
Huh?

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.510
Say, Yukina.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.880
I heard you guys went to the 
mainland during winter vacation.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.390
Did something happen?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.930
What do you mean by "something"?

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.430
She isn't like her own self.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.190
She seemed absent-minded during classes.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.650
Although it doesn't seem like she's sick.

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.460
I know!

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.550
Maybe it's because she couldn't eat crab cream croquette this time.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.110
Let's be serious.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.630
Nagisa-chan?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:26.380
What's wrong?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.440
Huh?

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.890
What, indeed.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.850
Sorry, I'm leaving now.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.410
She's jealous?

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.790
C'mon now.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:42.440
So this is where the transfer student was.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.780
I'll ask it frankly, Natsuki-chan.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.850
What's the deal with this chain?

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.090
Do not address your teacher with "chan."

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:04.460
It's because you ran off when I gently called out for you.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.750
Well, my body acted on its own.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.210
It was the working of my instincts.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.930
Anyway, you know what happened on New Year's Day.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.720
"New Year's Day..."?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.910
Well, what might you be talking about?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.310
Huh?

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.690
Uh, if you don't mind it then nor do I.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.020
At any rate, let's get to the point:

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.400
Astarte, show them the documents.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:29.610
Accepted.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.120
Are these?

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:37.040
The wrecked ships from yesterday?

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.580
The ones causing the cancelling of sailings bound for Itogami Island?

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:40.860
Negative.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:46.090
These all are the reports of the accidents that happened today from dawn until noon.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.700
All of these?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:48.550
Yes.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:51.800
If we only consider the ones 
in the reports, it's 21 accidents.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.050
Huh!?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.860
Having investigated the documents,

00:10:54.860 --> 00:11:00.310
the only thing in common we can say they have is that they were all bound to Itogami Island.

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:07.520
But due to these accidents, no goods have come to the island these past days, let alone people.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.900
Put another way, we can say that Itogami Island is more or less isolated at this point.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.780
I never thought the situation would be that bad.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:21.590
I think I now know why you chained Akatsuki-senpai up, Minamiya-sensei.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:25.790
You're suspecting him for whether this abnormality is his making, aren't you?

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:29.100
Hmph, I don't deny that.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.760
What?! Why's that?!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:36.220
There's a high chance these accidents are caused by magic barriers.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:42.430
And it wouldn't be way off to say that only a vampiric Progenitor has enough mana to pull this off.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.470
I thought I could put an end to it if I captured you.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:50.530
It ain't me and you know it!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:55.870
Then <i>hypothetically</i>, if Akatsuki Kojou is not its cause...

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:57.030
<i>Hypothetically,</i> now?!

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.990
Anyway, get this chain off me this instant!

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:03.960
I shall hear what you, a transfer student living as an anti-magical terrorism specialist, want to say.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:08.930
Do you have a lead for the deployment of a barrier of this scope?

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.920
If I had to bet, I'd say it's Feng Shui Technique.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:21.490
Shikisen{式占 I'm just making notes for myself--don't mind me}, where Feng Shui Technique originates in, is not only used for fortune-telling, but also as a large-scale occult art.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:26.630
One type of it is Hokimon{法奇門},
 one specially developed as an art of war.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:31.430
It's a military technique that 
controls the weather and the troops.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.870
"A military technique"?

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.110
For real?

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:36.650
Makes sense.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:41.170
If someone deployed the Eight Trigrams 
Formation using the long mai in the vicinity,{If someone deployed the Eight Trigrams Formation 八卦陣 using the whirlwinds and tornadoes in the vicinity,} {If someone deployed the Eight Trigrams Formation(八卦陣) using the long mai(龍脈 lit.: "dragon vein") in the vicinity,(in the novel: "using the long mai that flows in the ocean in the vicinity"}

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:45.400
bringing forth this situation is not impossible, I take it.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:53.290
Yes, but whether a geomancer who can control a formation of this scale without anyone noticing even exists...

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.590
Don't worry about that. I can think of <i>one</i> precedent.

00:12:56.590 --> 00:13:02.560
The annihilation incident in a special administrative region for demons in Iroise, Europe.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.720
"Iroise"?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:10.040
I recall it being a special administrative region for 
demons on the Atlantic Ocean, abandoned six years ago.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.780
But it was caused by flooding resulting from storms.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.910
At least that's what the public was told.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.740
But the facts are different.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:22.670
It was destroyed by an artificially crafted annihilation.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.320
By the hands of Tartarus Lapse.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:40.890
Carly.

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:44.570
The target's car is progressing along the anticipated route.{Previously used- The boss' car is progressing on the planned route.}{Xia ori tl- The car the target embarked on is progressing on the anticipated route.}{welli- The car the target took off in is progressing on the anticipated route.}{new welli- The target's car is progressing along the anticipated route.}

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:45.850
He'll arrive in a moment.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.550
Carly here.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.810
Target sighted.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.010
Preparing for sniping.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.600
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.270
I trust your judgment, Carly.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:55.730
Copy that.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.950
Much obliged, December.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.110
You're very much welcome.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.040
Target down confirmed.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.000
Proceeding to the next objective.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.670
Be swift or they'll catch your tail.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.630
"Tartarus Lapse"?

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:22.840
That's right.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:26.350
They're a subversive group of magic terrorists hired with money.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:32.940
One of their leaders is dubbed as a genius geomancer.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.440
Are you aware of that geomancer's background, Minamiya-sensei?

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.470
Senga Takehito.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:46.830
I think he'd be 40 years old now

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.800
He's one of the best Hokimon Users in the world.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:55.080
Can we break down the Eight Trigrams Formation once we find and capture him?

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.850
That would seem logical.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.430
Master, an urgent call from the Island Guards.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.440
All attack mages of the of Artificial Island Management Corporation

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.390
are to be notified that <i>Code Orange</i> is now active.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.720
Wha—?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.520
<i>Code Orange,</i> you say?!

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:19.480
It appears a higher-up of the company was killed by sniping.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.440
Huh?!

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:24.160
Their aim is to disturb the company's chain of command, huh?

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:27.180
It's certain now.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.110
It's terrorism.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.790
With the aim of causing mayhem on Itogami Island, and annihilating it.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.300
Indeed.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:42.200
Hurry up and confirm the identity of the sniper and their sniping point.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.510
And send escorts to all the high-salary leaders.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.260
Commander!

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:50.720
It appears two new aircraft had an accident.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.310
We just received new information about ship accidents.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.900
After all this, it simply leaves no doubt.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.910
Large-scale magic terrorism, I take it.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:03.860
You're noisy, Commander.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.530
Chairman Yaze, I am terribly sorry.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:15.500
If the person in charge of the organization
 isn't calm, the whole group will go into chaos.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.460
Maintain perfect composure.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.170
Where are you planning to go, Chairman?

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.970
After attending a conference
 with City Councilor Hashimura,

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:29.660
he plans to attend a memorial ceremony
 of the magic organization.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:30.810
But right now...

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:36.560
Are you trying to say I should be scared of some assassins, and shut myself behind the wall?

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.950
I will increase the security.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.230
Take utmost care of yourself.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:53.570
Commander, Attack Mage Minamiya reported something of interest.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.440
The Witch of the Void?

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:55.870
What is it?

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.730
Tartarus Lapse?!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.710
How come the Attack Magic Department didn't notice?

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:06.790
Related information are top secret.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.470
Their investigators are not authorized to access that information.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.220
Proceed to disclosure of information swiftly.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:16.610
And contact the Lion King Organization.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:19.490
They probably have spies on the island.

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.470
Make them cooperate, no matter what.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.820
Understood.

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.970
What should I do?

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.370
I can't face Kojou-kun like this.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:41.370
I can't take my eyes off him, and my heart goes pitter-patter whenever he looks at me.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:46.050
My chest start feeling very painful just by seeing him with a girl.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:50.490
Really, what <i>is</i> this feeling?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.760
I can't discuss this with anyone!

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:55.720
Here.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.430
Wanna eat it?

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.520
Lulua's ice cream tastes good.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:03.660
Huh?

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.900
Um, you are...

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:06.750
December.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:07.740
Huh?

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.870
December.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.990
That's my name.

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:11.870
I like it.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.370
I'll be happy if you call me that.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.830
I knew about that girl,

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:24.140
but to think we'd meet like this...

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.090
Guess it was fated.

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:29.300
It's tough for both of us.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:34.910
This is good!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:38.290
Um, December-san, what are you doing here?

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:41.140
I came to watch, you see.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:45.990
I said I'd watch over her, 
but she said it's not necessary.

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:50.490
I guess I'll watch while eating ice cream and pretending to just be sightseeing.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:53.600
Sightseeing the Keystone Gate?

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:55.950
Nuh-uh, I wouldn't say exactly.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:59.090
I came to see the beginning.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:03.080
The beginning of the end for the special administrative region for demons.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:10.540
What was that impact?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.070
It appears there was an explosion in the third basement parking lot.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:14.800
An <i>explosion</i>?!

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:20.180
Honorable Chairman Yaze Akishige's honorable car was in the third basement parking lot.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:26.400
Chairman Yaze's vital reading stopped.

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:30.860
The Keystone Gate...

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.970
Thou art...

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.510
It's all right.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:51.050
It's all right, don't worry.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:54.010
This is my war.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:01.050
For what reason have you waken me from my slumber?

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.430
Please...

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.790
Return to your slumber.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:21.330
That's <i>our</i> wish too.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.340
A bombing?!

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:30.610
"Missing"? Are you saying he got involved in <i>that</i>?

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:32.090
Are you serious, Brother?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.760
It's the truth.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:37.050
I'm still confused. I know nothing more.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:39.700
Let me investigate too.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.480
With my abilities...

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.070
Brother!

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:49.950
Yaze...

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.610
A notice to all of the students.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.610
Classes for today are suspended.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.970
All the students are requested to return home swiftly.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:01.830
Hey, Yaze!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:03.790
I'm leaving.

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:08.020
He must be shocked after hearing about the bombing.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:11.940
Yaze's father's an important person in the public corporation of management, after all.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.310
Tartarus Lapse, huh?

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:17.140
There's no way to think of it as someone else's problem anymore.

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:18.760
Tartar Sauce?

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.220
Do you know something, Kojou?

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:21.970
Uh, no.

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:24.810
You don't intend to keep things secret from me again, do you?

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.270
I got it...

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:38.410
So, both the explosion Motoki's father got involved in, <i>and</i> the cancelled ships are Tartar's doing?

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:40.240
It's called "Tartarus Lapse."

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.830
Natsuki-chan is after a geomancer called Senga.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:46.830
For now, he's the only member we're aware of.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:50.560
Tell it sooner next time.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.030
Can you find him?

00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:53.290
I <i>will</i> find him.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:21:59.010
Senpai!

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:00.210
Himeragi?

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:02.230
Why are you in school?

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:07.230
Nagisa-chan went out somewhere during lunch break alone, and she hasn't come back yet.

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:07.810
What?!

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.270
She's not answering texts either.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:11.230
Asagi.

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:12.880
All right, all right.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:15.630
I'll investigate her before the terrorists.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:17.110
Are you kidding?

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:19.570
Does this mean...?

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:21.160
Kojou, move it!

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:26.830
They got us, damn it!

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:28.620
A-Asagi?

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.200
They hacked us.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:33.690
Island Guard's network was contaminated by a virus.

00:22:33.690 --> 00:22:35.290
By the strong one they usually use against the military.

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:39.720
That... sounds pretty bad.

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:41.670
It <i>is</i> bad.

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.430
After all that happened, the chain of command was already in a confusion, and now this?

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:47.890
Senpai, don't tell me it was...?

00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:49.570
Tartarus Lapse, I bet.

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:55.150
<i>Where's Nagisa wandering about at a time like this?!</i>

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:03.070
Did you get an unrelated civilian involved?

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:09.570
Takehito, this girl just got scared from the explosion and fainted.

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:12.000
Of course I can't leave such a cutie alone.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.120
Bad guys would kidnap her.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:18.580
You're one to talk.

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:21.440
Would <i>you</i> leave her?

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:25.030
You're not unrelated to this island either, are you?

00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:29.600
Especially because I'm not unrelated, there are things I can't allow.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.410
I see.

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:32.730
It figures.

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:35.060
That's why I'm putting an end to this.

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:38.520
By the Rose of Tartarus.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:46.140
Huh?

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:48.910
Why am I here—?

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:51.490
I-I-I'm sorry!

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:52.550
Excuse me!

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:54.640
To think I'd get a lap pillow...!

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:55.780
A call.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:56.550
Huh?

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:58.390
You got a call.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:23:59.340
You're right.

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:03.050
Kojou-kun, why?

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:05.630
Damn, that Nagisa...

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.830
It looks like she <i>unknowingly</i> took a nap,
 because of the nice weather.

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:10.850
My ass!

00:24:11.310 --> 00:24:13.120
It's good that she is safe, at least.

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:15.130
You're right.

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:18.310
But to think everyone's still acting normal.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:23.780
Well, residents of the special administrative region for demons are used to disturbances like this.

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:32.200
I just hope Asagi and Mogwai finds some clues on Senga before anything else happens.

00:24:32.590 --> 00:24:34.210
Me too.

00:24:34.210 --> 00:24:36.670
Sorry, Kojou-kun!

00:24:38.140 --> 00:24:39.670
Thanks for seeing me off.

00:24:40.130 --> 00:24:41.470
Nagisa-chan!

00:24:41.470 --> 00:24:43.550
Hey, Nagisa, who's that girl?

00:24:43.990 --> 00:24:48.710
Um, we met in the park, and she kindly took me here.

00:24:48.710 --> 00:24:51.060
Are you Nagisa-chan's Onii-san?

00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.020
Just call me "December".

00:24:54.730 --> 00:24:55.930
Nice to meet you.

00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:05.320
Senpai?

00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:06.530
Kojou-kun?

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:15.820
You're Avrora...
